Q: JPA aur Hibernate mein kya difference hai?

────────────────────────────────────────
One-line

JPA = specification (standard API / interfaces + annotations)
Hibernate = most popular implementation (actual ORM framework that implements JPA)

JPA = “rules / contract”
Hibernate = “engine that follows those rules” (and adds extras)

────────────────────────────────────────
Comparison

| Point            | JPA                                      | Hibernate                                      |
| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| What is it?      | Spec / API (Jakarta Persistence)         | ORM framework / JPA provider                   |
| Alone usable?    | No — needs an implementation             | Yes (native API) + as JPA provider             |
| Package          | jakarta.persistence.*                    | org.hibernate.* (+ implements JPA)             |
| Query language   | JPQL                                     | HQL (similar) + native SQL + Criteria          |
| Who defines it?  | Jakarta EE                               | Red Hat / Hibernate community                  |
| Spring Boot      | Spring Data JPA uses JPA APIs            | Default provider under spring-boot-starter-data-jpa |

────────────────────────────────────────
How they work together in Spring Boot

Your code (JPA annotations / EntityManager / Spring Data)
                    ↓
              Hibernate (provider)
                    ↓
                 JDBC / HikariCP
                    ↓
                 Database

You mostly write JPA-style code:
@Entity, @Id, EntityManager, @Query (JPQL)

Hibernate does the real SQL generation, caching (L1/L2), dirty checking, etc.

────────────────────────────────────────
Extra Hibernate features (beyond plain JPA)

- Better caching controls / L2 cache integrations
- Hibernate-specific annotations (@Cache, @BatchSize, @Filter, …)
- HQL extensions / StatelessSession
- More tuning / statistics

Rule of thumb:
Prefer portable JPA APIs in app code; use Hibernate-specific features only when needed.

────────────────────────────────────────
✅ Short Interview Answer

JPA ek standard specification hai jo batati hai entities ko DB se kaise map karna hai.
Hibernate us specification ka implementation hai — actual ORM jo SQL generate karta hai.
Spring Boot mein hum JPA annotations use karte hain; peeche default provider Hibernate hota hai.
JPA = interface/standard; Hibernate = implementation.
